completion:
This is Effect 3.x, where `Either` no longer exposes `.left`/`.right` directly — use `Either` helpers instead.

```ts
import {Effect, Either} from 'effect';
import {goTo, hunt, disengage, note} from 'play';

export default Effect.gen(function* () {
  yield* goTo('sol_nebula');
  const result = yield* Effect.either(hunt({fights: 2}));
  yield* disengage();
  if (Either.isLeft(result)) {
    yield* Effect.fail(result.value);
  }
  yield* note(`hunt ended: ${result.value.ended} (${result.value.fights.length} fights)`);
});
```

`Either.either` folds both branches into the success channel with the inner value at `.value`; `Either.isLeft` discriminates. On a failure I re-raise it via `Effect.fail`, so the program still fails — but only after `disengage()` has run.

