The error is because `Schedule.exponential`'s first argument in this Effect version is a `Duration` (it treats `1_000` as raw milliseconds), so passing an options object isn't accepted. I'll build the backoff via `Schedule.exponential` (in ms) piped through `Schedule.recurs(5)` — starting at 1 second, doubling each retry, capped at 5 retries (6 attempts total).

```ts
import {Effect, Schedule} from 'effect';
import {goTo, note} from 'play';

/**
 * goTo wrapped with retry-on-ServerBusy: exponential backoff starting at 1 second
 * (doubling each time), at most 5 retries (6 attempts in all).
 * Every other error fails the program as-is.
 */
const go = (id: string) =>
  goTo(id).pipe(
    Effect.retry({
      // Only the transient ServerBusy error is retried; anything else is
      // thrown (to the runtime) instead of fed back into the schedule.
      while: (e): boolean => e._tag === 'ServerBusy',
      // Exponential backoff in ms (1s → 2s → 4s …), capped after 5 retries.
      schedule: Schedule.exponential(1_000).pipe(Schedule.recurs(5)),
    }),
  );

export default Effect.gen(function* () {
  yield* go('sol_belt');
  yield* note('docked at sol_belt');
});
```

